  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: 3rd person -s",
      "title_form": "Presente simple: la -s de la tercera persona",
      "title_target": "Present Simple: The 3rd Person -s",
      "description_md_form": "En inglés, cuando hablamos de **él**, **ella** o **eso** (he, she, it), el verbo en presente simple lleva una **-s** al final. Es una regla fija: no la olvides.\n\n- `I put on` → **He puts on**\n- `I wear` → **She wears**\n- `I go out` → **It goes out**\n\nEsta -s solo aparece con la tercera persona del singular. Con `I`, `you`, `we` y `they`, el verbo no cambia.\n\n**Ejemplo:**\n- *She puts on her coat and goes out.* (Ella se pone el abrigo y sale.)\n\n**Ojo:** con verbos que terminan en `-o`, `-s`, `-x`, `-ch`, `-sh`, agregamos `-es`: `go` → `goes`. Con verbos que terminan en consonante + `-y`, cambiamos la `-y` por `-ies`: `study` → `studies`.",
      "description_md_target": "In English, when we talk about **he**, **she**, or **it**, the verb in the present simple takes an **-s** at the end. It is a fixed rule: do not forget it.\n\n- `I put on` → **He puts on**\n- `I wear` → **She wears**\n- `I go out` → **It goes out**\n\nThis -s only appears with the third person singular. With `I`, `you`, `we`, and `they`, the verb does not change.\n\n**Example:**\n- *She puts on her coat and goes out.*\n\n**Note:** with verbs ending in `-o`, `-s`, `-x`, `-ch`, `-sh`, we add `-es`: `go` → `goes`. With verbs ending in consonant + `-y`, we change the `-y` to `-ies`: `study` → `studies`.",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject (he/she/it) + verb + -s",
